  "notes": {
    "c0001.md": "# Delia Marchetti, Northgate Logistics\n\nMonth twelve. 9000 a month against a book of 16200, so Northgate is 55 percent\nof the business. If Delia leaves, two of the three remaining retainers do not\ncover the desk, the insurance and the tax.\n\n- Renewal is a decision on both sides. Reprice at 9800 and cap the standing\n  calls at two a week, or the unbilled hours carry into month eighteen.\n- Dev Anand approves the invoices. He pays the retainer line without reading it\n  and queries every line above it. Anything out of scope goes on its own invoice\n  with the hours listed, or it does not get paid.\n- Five and a half hours last month never reached a time entry.\n",
    "p0003.md": "# Cotter retainer, month 3\n\nSold as a Friday review at 3200 a month, thirteen hours. Week one it was a\nMonday check in as well. Week three it is a daily call and a shift board rebuild\nnobody agreed to.\n\nMonth three: fifteen and a half hours logged, four of them unbillable, and the\nmonth is not over. At 165 an hour the retainer returns 14 percent against a 62\npercent target.\n\nThe fix is one sentence in writing to Priyanka: the daily call is out of scope,\nit ends Friday, and the shift board is month four work at month four prices.\nSay it once. Do not say it on the call.\n"
  }
